    {
      "name": "com.facebook.sdk",
      "latestFrom": "meta/facebook-sdk-for-unity",
      "tarball": "https://github.com/meta/facebook-sdk-for-unity/releases/download/sdk-version-{version}/facebook-unity-sdk-{version}.zip",
      "unitypackage": "facebook-unity-sdk-{version}/FacebookSDK/facebook-unity-sdk-{version}.unitypackage",
      "licence": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/meta/facebook-sdk-for-unity/sdk-version-{version}/LICENSE.txt",
      "take": {
        "Assets/FacebookSDK/Plugins/": "Plugins/",
        "Assets/FacebookSDK/SDK/": "SDK/",
        "Assets/FacebookSDK/link.xml": "link.xml",
        "Assets/Editor/": "Editor/",
        "Assets/FacebookSDK/Examples/": "Samples~/Examples/",
        "Assets/IAPiOS/IAP/": "Samples~/Examples/IAP/",
        "Assets/Scripts/": "Samples~/Examples/IAP/Scripts/",
        "Assets/StreamingAssets/": "Samples~/Examples/StreamingAssets/"
      },
      "leaveOut": [
        "Assets/ExternalDependencyManager/"
      ],
      "metaLike": {
        "Plugins/Windows/XInputDotNetPure.dll": "Plugins/Windows/LibFBGManaged.dll",
        "Plugins/Windows/x64/XInputInterface.dll": "Plugins/Windows/x64/zlib1.dll",
        "Plugins/Windows/x86/XInputInterface.dll": "Plugins/Windows/x86/zlib1.dll"
      },
      "changes": [
        "- Made into a Unity package from Meta's `.unitypackage`. All of Meta's files are here. The only thing left out is Google's External Dependency Manager, which Meta bundles and Google has deprecated.",
        "- Meta's examples, the IAP sample they call and the StreamingAssets files they read are under **Samples** in the Package Manager window, so they only enter a project when you import them.",
        "- `package.json` is new and depends on `com.unity.external-dependency-manager`.",
        "- `Editor/Facebook.Unity.PostProcess.asmdef` is new, because Unity compiles no script in a package without one.",
        "- `Editor/FacebookLinkFile.cs` is new, because Unity reads no `link.xml` from inside a package.",
        "- The `.meta` files of `XInputDotNetPure.dll` and the two `XInputInterface.dll` now say what Meta's `FacebookImporter` sets, because that importer does nothing to files in a package."
      ],
      "links": {
        "documentationUrl": "https://developers.facebook.com/documentation/unity",
        "changelogUrl": "https://github.com/meta/facebook-sdk-for-unity/blob/sdk-version-{version}/CHANGELOG.md",
        "licensesUrl": "https://github.com/meta/facebook-sdk-for-unity/blob/sdk-version-{version}/LICENSE.txt"
      }
    },
